module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.CoproductInclusion
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.UliftYonedaCoproduct

/-!
# Coproducts in the big fppf site and their representable sheaves

A big fppf site contains the coproduct of any family of its schemes indexed by an *admissible*
index type — `u`-small, of cardinality below the cofinality of the size cutoff — because the
cutoff is a strong prelimit of uncountable cofinality. Consequently the big fppf site of `S`
has such coproducts, computed on underlying schemes, and — this is the point — the
representable *sheaf* of such a coproduct is the coproduct of the representable sheaves.

The last statement is the mechanism behind the atlas of a coproduct of algebraic spaces: if
`U i ⟶ F i` are surjective étale atlases and `V = ∐ U i` lies in the site, then a morphism
`h_V ⟶ ∐ F i` of sheaves is exactly a family of morphisms `h_{U i} ⟶ ∐ F i`, so the atlases
assemble into a single morphism out of a representable sheaf. Stacks 02WQ calls this
"straightforward to verify"; it is the content of
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.isColimit_yoneda_cofan`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfSite.AdmitsCoproductIndex`: the admissibility condition on an
  index type, satisfied by every countable one.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfSite.contains_sigma`: a big fppf site contains the coproduct of an
  admissibly indexed family of its schemes.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.isColimit_sigmaCofan`: the explicit coproduct of the big fppf
  site of `S`, computed on underlying schemes.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.isColimit_yoneda_sigmaCofan` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.isColimit_yoneda_cofan`: the representable sheaf of such a
  coproduct of the site is the coproduct of the representable sheaves, for the explicit
  coproduct and for an arbitrary colimiting cofan respectively.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.isColimitUliftYonedaSigmaCofan`: the same statement for the
  universe-raising Yoneda embedding, which is the form the theory of formal algebraic spaces
  needs, its sheaves taking values one universe above the morphisms of the site.

## Implementation notes

The index type is allowed to live in an arbitrary universe, as the statement of Stacks 02WQ
does; `u`-smallness, which the coproduct of schemes needs, is part of admissibility. The
covering families of a big fppf site are indexed in `Type (u+1)`, so the Zariski covering by
the summands is formed over a `Type (u+1)` copy of the index type and the resulting covering
sieve is compared with the sieve generated by the cofan through
`CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.superset_covering`; only the easy inclusion is needed,
since every arrow of the reindexed family is literally an arrow of the original one.

`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.isColimit_yoneda_sigmaCofan` is the descent criterion
`CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.isColimitCofanMkYoneda` for a covering family of
monomorphisms with initial pairwise intersections, exactly as in the case of `S ⨿ S` treated
in `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/CoproductInclusion.lean`; the disjointness input is
Mathlib's `AlgebraicGeometry.isEmpty_pullback_sigmaι_of_ne`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 02WQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02WQ)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite Cardinal

universe u v

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- A cofan transported along an isomorphism of its vertex is again colimiting. -/
noncomputable def Cofan.isColimitOfIso {C : Type*} [Category C] {I : Type v} {X : I → C}
    {P Q : C} {p : ∀ i, X i ⟶ P} {q : ∀ i, X i ⟶ Q} (hp : IsColimit (Cofan.mk P p))
    (e : P ≅ Q) (hq : ∀ i, p i ≫ e.hom = q i) : IsColimit (Cofan.mk Q q) :=
  hp.ofIsoColimit (Cofan.ext e hq)

/-- An index type **admissible for coproducts** in a big fppf site `B`: it is `u`-small, and
its cardinality lies below the cofinality of `B`'s size cutoff.

Those two conditions are what bounds the size of a coproduct indexed by it, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.schemeSize_coproduct_le`: smallness so that the coproduct of schemes
exists at all, and the cofinality bound so that the *supremum* of the component sizes is
below the cutoff, each component being below it.

The cofinality bound, rather than the weaker `#I < B.cutoff`, is what an arbitrary family
needs: a supremum of `#I` many cardinals each below the cutoff exceeds it as soon as `#I`
reaches its cofinality. A family carrying a *uniform* size bound needs only `#I < B.cutoff`,
directly from `AlgebraicGeometry.schemeSize_coproduct_le`; but no such bound is available
for the families this development forms, whose members are representing objects produced by
an existential and are therefore known only to lie in the site.

Every *finite* index type is admissible, and so is every small index type of cardinality below
`cof (B.cutoff.ord)`, which `B` axiomatises only as being greater than `ℵ₀`. -/
class BigFppfSite.AdmitsCoproductIndex (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (I : Type v)
    [Small.{u} I] : Prop where
  /-- The cardinality of the index, read on its canonical `u`-small copy, is below the
  cofinality of the cutoff. -/
  mk_shrink_lt_cutoff_cof : #(Shrink.{u} I) < B.cutoff.ord.cof

/-- Every finite index type is admissible for coproducts in a big fppf site. -/
instance BigFppfSite.admitsCoproductIndex_of_finite (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (I : Type v)
    [Finite I] : B.AdmitsCoproductIndex I :=
  have _ : Finite (Shrink.{u} I) := Finite.of_equiv _ (equivShrink.{u} I)
  ⟨Cardinal.mk_le_aleph0.trans_lt B.aleph0_lt_cutoff_cof⟩

/-- Every countable index type is admissible: its cardinality is at most `ℵ₀`, which is below
the cofinality of the cutoff. These are the coproducts that Stacks 000R(2) puts in the
category of schemes underlying a big site. -/
instance BigFppfSite.admitsCoproductIndex_of_countable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (I : Type v)
    [Small.{u} I] [Countable I] : B.AdmitsCoproductIndex I :=
  have _ : Countable (Shrink.{u} I) := (equivShrink.{u} I).symm.injective.countable
  ⟨Cardinal.mk_le_aleph0.trans_lt B.aleph0_lt_cutoff_cof⟩

/-- A big fppf site contains the coproduct of an admissible family of schemes it contains:
its size cutoff has cofinality above the cardinality of the index, so the index and the
supremum of the component sizes are both below it, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.schemeSize_coproduct_le` bounds the coproduct by their maximum.

The index type may live in any universe; admissibility makes it `u`-small. -/
theorem BigFppfSite.contains_sigma (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) {I : Type v} [Small.{u} I]
    [h : B.AdmitsCoproductIndex I] (X : I → Scheme.{u}) (hX : ∀ i, B.Contains (X i)) :
    B.Contains (∐ X) := by
  have hI : #(Shrink.{u} I) < B.cutoff.ord.cof := h.mk_shrink_lt_cutoff_cof
  let Y : Shrink.{u} I → Scheme.{u} := fun k => X ((equivShrink.{u} I).symm k)
  have hcut : max (max ℵ₀ #(Shrink.{u} I)) (⨆ k, (Y k).size) < B.cutoff :=
    max_lt (max_lt B.aleph0_lt_cutoff (hI.trans_le (Ordinal.cof_ord_le _)))
      (Cardinal.iSup_lt_of_lt_cof_ord hI fun k => hX _)
  have hY : (∐ Y).size ≤ max (max ℵ₀ #(Shrink.{u} I)) (⨆ k, (Y k).size) :=
    schemeSize_coproduct_le Y _ ((le_max_left _ _).trans (le_max_left _ _))
      ((le_max_right _ _).trans (le_max_left _ _))
      fun k => (le_ciSup Cardinal.bddAbove_of_small k).trans (le_max_right _ _)
  have e : (∐ X) ≅ ∐ Y :=
    Sigma.whiskerEquiv (equivShrink.{u} I) fun i => eqToIso (by simp [Y])
  change (∐ X).size < B.cutoff
  rw [Scheme.size_congr e]
  exact hY.trans_lt hcut

namespace BigFppfOver

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
  {I : Type v} [Small.{u} I] [B.AdmitsCoproductIndex I] (U : I → BigFppfOver B S hS)

/-- The coproduct of the underlying schemes of an admissibly indexed family of objects of the
big fppf site of `S` is contained in the site. -/
theorem contains_sigma_toScheme :
    B.Contains (∐ fun i => (toScheme B S hS).obj (U i)) :=
  B.contains_sigma _ fun i => (U i).left.property

/-- The coproduct of a family of objects of the big fppf site of `S`, with underlying
scheme the coproduct of their underlying schemes. -/
noncomputable def sigmaObj : BigFppfOver B S hS :=
  Over.mk (B.inclusion.preimage (X := B.obj (contains_sigma_toScheme B S hS U))
    (Y := B.obj hS) (Sigma.desc fun i => B.inclusion.map (U i).hom))

/-- The `i`-th inclusion into the coproduct of a family of objects of the big fppf
site of `S`. -/
noncomputable def sigmaIncl (i : I) : U i ⟶ sigmaObj B S hS U :=
  Over.homMk (B.inclusion.preimage (X := (U i).left)
    (Y := B.obj (contains_sigma_toScheme B S hS U))
    (Sigma.ι (fun i => (toScheme B S hS).obj (U i)) i)) (by
    apply B.inclusion.map_injective
    change B.inclusion.map (B.inclusion.preimage (X := (U i).left)
        (Y := B.obj (contains_sigma_toScheme B S hS U))
        (Sigma.ι (fun i => (toScheme B S hS).obj (U i)) i) ≫
      B.inclusion.preimage (X := B.obj (contains_sigma_toScheme B S hS U)) (Y := B.obj hS)
        (Sigma.desc fun i => B.inclusion.map (U i).hom)) = _
    rw [Functor.map_comp, B.inclusion.map_preimage, B.inclusion.map_preimage]
    exact Sigma.ι_comp_desc _ i)

/-- The underlying scheme morphism of the `i`-th inclusion into the coproduct. -/
theorem sigmaIncl_left_hom (i : I) :
    (sigmaIncl B S hS U i).left.hom =
      Sigma.ι (fun i => (toScheme B S hS).obj (U i)) i := by
  change B.inclusion.map (B.inclusion.preimage (X := (U i).left)
    (Y := B.obj (contains_sigma_toScheme B S hS U))
    (Sigma.ι (fun i => (toScheme B S hS).obj (U i)) i)) = _
  exact B.inclusion.map_preimage _

/-- The underlying scheme morphism of the `i`-th inclusion into the coproduct, read through
the functor to schemes. -/
theorem toScheme_map_sigmaIncl (i : I) :
    (toScheme B S hS).map (sigmaIncl B S hS U i) =
      Sigma.ι (fun i => (toScheme B S hS).obj (U i)) i :=
  sigmaIncl_left_hom B S hS U i

/-- The cofan of a family of objects of the big fppf site of `S` given by its
coproduct. -/
noncomputable def sigmaCofan : Cofan U := Cofan.mk (sigmaObj B S hS U) (sigmaIncl B S hS U)

/-- The injections of the coproduct cofan are the coproduct inclusions. -/
theorem sigmaCofan_inj (i : I) : (sigmaCofan B S hS U).inj i = sigmaIncl B S hS U i := rfl

/-- The coproduct of a family of objects of the big fppf site of `S` is a coproduct in
the site: the site is a slice of a full subcategory of schemes closed under such
coproducts, so the coproduct is computed on underlying schemes. -/
noncomputable def isColimit_sigmaCofan : IsColimit (sigmaCofan B S hS U) := by
  let X : I → Scheme.{u} := fun i => (toScheme B S hS).obj (U i)
  let hcScheme : IsColimit (Cofan.mk (∐ X) (fun i => Sigma.ι X i)) :=
    coproductIsCoproduct X
  let cSite : Cofan (fun i => (U i).left) :=
    Cofan.mk (B.obj (contains_sigma_toScheme B S hS U))
      fun i => B.inclusion.preimage (Sigma.ι X i)
  have hκ (i : I) : B.inclusion.map (cSite.inj i) = Sigma.ι X i :=
    B.inclusion.map_preimage _
  have hcSite : IsColimit cSite := by
    refine Cofan.IsColimit.mk cSite (fun t => B.inclusion.preimage
      (hcScheme.desc (Cofan.mk (B.inclusion.obj t.pt)
        fun i => B.inclusion.map (t.inj i)))) ?_ ?_
    · intro t i
      apply B.inclusion.map_injective
      rw [Functor.map_comp, B.inclusion.map_preimage, hκ]
      exact Cofan.IsColimit.inj_desc _ hcScheme i
    · intro t m hm
      apply B.inclusion.map_injective
      rw [B.inclusion.map_preimage]
      refine Cofan.IsColimit.hom_ext hcScheme _ _ fun i => ?_
      calc
        Sigma.ι X i ≫ B.inclusion.map m
            = B.inclusion.map (cSite.inj i) ≫ B.inclusion.map m := by rw [hκ]
        _ = B.inclusion.map (t.inj i) := by rw [← Functor.map_comp, hm i]
        _ = Sigma.ι X i ≫ hcScheme.desc (Cofan.mk (B.inclusion.obj t.pt)
            fun j => B.inclusion.map (t.inj j)) := by
          symm
          exact Cofan.IsColimit.inj_desc _ hcScheme i
  let d (t : Cofan U) : (sigmaObj B S hS U).left ⟶ t.pt.left :=
    hcSite.desc (Cofan.mk t.pt.left fun i => (t.inj i).left)
  have hfac (t : Cofan U) (i : I) : cSite.inj i ≫ d t = (t.inj i).left :=
    Cofan.IsColimit.fac hcSite (fun k => (t.inj k).left) i
  have hdw (t : Cofan U) : d t ≫ t.pt.hom = (sigmaObj B S hS U).hom := by
    refine Cofan.IsColimit.hom_ext hcSite _ _ fun i => ?_
    calc
      cSite.inj i ≫ d t ≫ t.pt.hom = (cSite.inj i ≫ d t) ≫ t.pt.hom := by
        rw [Category.assoc]
      _ = (t.inj i).left ≫ t.pt.hom := by rw [hfac]
      _ = (U i).hom := (t.inj i).w
      _ = cSite.inj i ≫ (sigmaObj B S hS U).hom := (sigmaIncl B S hS U i).w.symm
  refine Cofan.IsColimit.mk _ (fun t => Over.homMk (d t) (hdw t)) ?_ ?_
  · exact fun t i => Over.OverMorphism.ext (hfac t i)
  · intro t m hm
    apply Over.OverMorphism.ext
    refine Cofan.IsColimit.hom_ext hcSite _ _ fun i => ?_
    calc
      cSite.inj i ≫ m.left = (t.inj i).left :=
        congrArg (fun q : U i ⟶ t.pt => q.left) (hm i)
      _ = cSite.inj i ≫ d t := (hfac t i).symm

/-- A copy of a `u`-small index type in the universe in which the covering families of a big
fppf site are indexed. -/
noncomputable def sigmaIndexEquiv (I : Type v) [Small.{u} I] :
    ULift.{u + 1} (Shrink.{u} I) ≃ I := Equiv.ulift.trans (equivShrink.{u} I).symm

/-- The summands of a coproduct of the big fppf site of `S`, as a covering family of
it, indexed in the universe of the site's covering families. -/
noncomputable def sigmaCover : PreZeroHypercover (sigmaObj B S hS U) where
  I₀ := ULift.{u + 1} (Shrink.{u} I)
  X k := U (sigmaIndexEquiv I k)
  f k := sigmaIncl B S hS U (sigmaIndexEquiv I k)

/-- The underlying scheme of a coproduct of the big fppf site of `S`. -/
theorem toScheme_obj_sigmaObj :
    (toScheme B S hS).obj (sigmaObj B S hS U) =
      ∐ fun i => (toScheme B S hS).obj (U i) := rfl

/-- The presieve of the covering family by the summands of a coproduct. -/
theorem sigmaCover_presieve₀ : (sigmaCover B S hS U).presieve₀ =
    Presieve.ofArrows (fun k : ULift.{u + 1} (Shrink.{u} I) => U (sigmaIndexEquiv I k))
      (fun k => sigmaIncl B S hS U (sigmaIndexEquiv I k)) := rfl

/-- The summands of a coproduct of the big fppf site of `S` form a Zariski, hence
fppf, covering family of it. -/
theorem isFppfCovering_sigmaCover :
    IsFppfCovering ⟨(sigmaObj B S hS U).left,
      (sigmaCover B S hS U).map (Over.forget (B.obj hS))⟩ := by
  have hsurj : ∀ x : ((∐ fun i => (toScheme B S hS).obj (U i) : Scheme.{u}) : Type u),
      ∃ i : I, x ∈ Set.range (Sigma.ι (fun i => (toScheme B S hS).obj (U i)) i) := by
    intro x
    obtain ⟨i, y, hy⟩ := (sigmaOpenCover fun i => (toScheme B S hS).obj (U i)).exists_eq x
    exact ⟨i, y, by rwa [← sigmaOpenCover_f (fun i => (toScheme B S hS).obj (U i)) i]⟩
  have hZ : Presieve.ofArrows
      (fun k : ULift.{u + 1} (Shrink.{u} I) =>
        (toScheme B S hS).obj (U (sigmaIndexEquiv I k)))
      (fun k => Sigma.ι (fun i => (toScheme B S hS).obj (U i)) (sigmaIndexEquiv I k)) ∈
      Scheme.zariskiPrecoverage (∐ fun i => (toScheme B S hS).obj (U i)) := by
    apply (Scheme.ofArrows_mem_precoverage_iff
      (@IsOpenImmersion.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})).2
    refine ⟨fun x => ?_, fun _ => inferInstance⟩
    obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := hsurj x
    exact ⟨(sigmaIndexEquiv I).symm i, by rwa [Equiv.apply_symm_apply]⟩
  have hmaps : ∀ k : ULift.{u + 1} (Shrink.{u} I),
      (schemeBelowInclusion B.cutoff).map ((Over.forget (B.obj hS)).map
          (sigmaIncl B S hS U (sigmaIndexEquiv I k))) =
        Sigma.ι (fun i => (toScheme B S hS).obj (U i)) (sigmaIndexEquiv I k) :=
    fun k => toScheme_map_sigmaIncl B S hS U _
  unfold IsFppfCovering
  rw [Precoverage.mem_comap_iff, PreZeroHypercover.presieve₀_map, sigmaCover_presieve₀,
    Presieve.map_ofArrows, Presieve.map_ofArrows]
  simp only [hmaps]
  exact Scheme.zariskiPrecoverage_le_fppfPrecoverage _ hZ

/-- The sieve generated by the summands of a coproduct of the big fppf site of `S`
covers it. -/
theorem sieve_sigmaCofan_mem_topology :
    Sieve.ofArrows U (sigmaCofan B S hS U).inj ∈
      BigFppfOver.topology B S hS (sigmaObj B S hS U) := by
  have hgen := B.generate_mem_topology_of_isFppfCovering
    ((sigmaCover B S hS U).map (Over.forget (B.obj hS)))
    (isFppfCovering_sigmaCover B S hS U)
  have hre : Sieve.ofArrows (fun k : ULift.{u + 1} (Shrink.{u} I) => U (sigmaIndexEquiv I k))
      (fun k => sigmaIncl B S hS U (sigmaIndexEquiv I k)) ∈
      BigFppfOver.topology B S hS (sigmaObj B S hS U) := by
    have heq : Sieve.ofArrows
          (fun k : ULift.{u + 1} (Shrink.{u} I) => U (sigmaIndexEquiv I k))
          (fun k => sigmaIncl B S hS U (sigmaIndexEquiv I k)) =
        (Sieve.overEquiv (sigmaObj B S hS U)).symm (Sieve.ofArrows
          (fun k : ULift.{u + 1} (Shrink.{u} I) => (U (sigmaIndexEquiv I k)).left)
          (fun k => (sigmaIncl B S hS U (sigmaIndexEquiv I k)).left)) := by
      apply (Sieve.overEquiv (sigmaObj B S hS U)).injective
      rw [OrderIso.apply_symm_apply]
      exact Sieve.overEquiv_ofArrows _ _
    rw [heq]
    apply B.topology.overEquiv_symm_mem_over
    simpa [sigmaCover, PreZeroHypercover.presieve₀_map,
      Sieve.functorPushforward_overForget_arrows, BigFppfOver.forget] using hgen
  refine (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS).superset_covering ?_ hre
  apply (Sieve.generate_le_iff _ _).2
  rintro Y g ⟨k⟩
  exact Sieve.ofArrows_mk U (sigmaCofan B S hS U).inj (sigmaIndexEquiv I k)

/-- **The atlas mechanism of Stacks 02WQ.** The representable sheaf of the explicit coproduct
of the big fppf site of `S` is the coproduct, in sheaves, of the representable sheaves of the
summands. -/
noncomputable def isColimit_yoneda_sigmaCofan
    [(BigFppfOver.topology B S hS).Subcanonical] :
    IsColimit (Cofan.mk ((BigFppfOver.topology B S hS).yoneda.obj (sigmaObj B S hS U))
      fun i => (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS).yoneda.map (sigmaIncl B S hS U i)) := by
  let J := BigFppfOver.topology B S hS
  have hmono : ∀ i, Mono ((sigmaCofan B S hS U).inj i) := by
    intro i
    rw [sigmaCofan_inj]
    apply (Over.forget (B.obj hS)).mono_of_mono_map
    apply B.inclusion.mono_of_mono_map
    change Mono ((toScheme B S hS).map (sigmaIncl B S hS U i))
    rw [toScheme_map_sigmaIncl]
    exact inferInstanceAs (Mono (Sigma.ι (fun i => (toScheme B S hS).obj (U i)) i))
  let _ : ∀ i, Mono ((sigmaCofan B S hS U).inj i) := hmono
  exact J.isColimitCofanMkYoneda (c := sigmaCofan B S hS U) U
    (sieve_sigmaCofan_mem_topology B S hS U)
    (bot_mem_topology_of_isInitial B S hS)
    (by
      intro i j hij Y a b hab
      have hab' : (toScheme B S hS).map a ≫
            Sigma.ι (fun i => (toScheme B S hS).obj (U i)) i =
          (toScheme B S hS).map b ≫
            Sigma.ι (fun i => (toScheme B S hS).obj (U i)) j := by
        have h : (toScheme B S hS).map (a ≫ sigmaIncl B S hS U i) =
            (toScheme B S hS).map (b ≫ sigmaIncl B S hS U j) :=
          congrArg (toScheme B S hS).map hab
        rw [← toScheme_map_sigmaIncl B S hS U i, ← toScheme_map_sigmaIncl B S hS U j]
        exact ((toScheme B S hS).map_comp a (sigmaIncl B S hS U i)).symm.trans
          (h.trans ((toScheme B S hS).map_comp b (sigmaIncl B S hS U j)))
      have hempty : IsEmpty ((toScheme B S hS).obj Y) :=
        isEmpty_of_commSq_sigmaι_of_ne ⟨hab'⟩ hij
      exact ⟨Over.isInitialOfIsInitialLeft (Y := Y)
        (isInitial_schemeBelow B (isInitial_iff_isEmpty.mpr hempty).some)⟩)

/-- **The representable sheaf of a coproduct of the big fppf site of `S` is the coproduct of
the representable sheaves**, in sheaves of types one universe above the morphisms of the site.

This is `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.isColimit_yoneda_sigmaCofan` with the value universe of
the sheaves raised, which is the only form the theory of formal algebraic spaces can use: a
formal algebraic space over `S` is a sheaf of `Type (u + 1)` while the morphisms of the site
are in `Type u`. The descent input is the universe-raised descent criterion
`CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.isColimitCofanMkUliftYoneda`, and the covering and
disjointness data are the same as in the unraised statement. -/
noncomputable def isColimitUliftYonedaSigmaCofan
    [(BigFppfOver.topology B S hS).Subcanonical] :
    IsColimit (Cofan.mk
      ((BigFppfOver.topology B S hS).uliftYoneda.{u + 1}.obj (sigmaObj B S hS U))
      fun i ↦ (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS).uliftYoneda.{u + 1}.map
        (sigmaIncl B S hS U i)) := by
  have hmono : ∀ i, Mono ((sigmaCofan B S hS U).inj i) := by
    intro i
    rw [sigmaCofan_inj]
    refine (Over.forget (B.obj hS)).mono_of_mono_map (B.inclusion.mono_of_mono_map ?_)
    change Mono ((toScheme B S hS).map (sigmaIncl B S hS U i))
    rw [toScheme_map_sigmaIncl]
    exact inferInstanceAs (Mono (Sigma.ι (fun i ↦ (toScheme B S hS).obj (U i)) i))
  let _ : ∀ i, Mono ((sigmaCofan B S hS U).inj i) := hmono
  exact (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS).isColimitCofanMkUliftYoneda.{u + 1} U
    (c := sigmaCofan B S hS U) (sieve_sigmaCofan_mem_topology B S hS U)
    (bot_mem_topology_of_isInitial B S hS)
    (by
      intro i j hij Y x y hxy
      have hxy' : (toScheme B S hS).map x ≫ Sigma.ι (fun i ↦ (toScheme B S hS).obj (U i)) i =
          (toScheme B S hS).map y ≫ Sigma.ι (fun i ↦ (toScheme B S hS).obj (U i)) j := by
        have h : (toScheme B S hS).map (x ≫ sigmaIncl B S hS U i) =
            (toScheme B S hS).map (y ≫ sigmaIncl B S hS U j) :=
          congrArg (toScheme B S hS).map hxy
        rw [← toScheme_map_sigmaIncl B S hS U i, ← toScheme_map_sigmaIncl B S hS U j]
        exact ((toScheme B S hS).map_comp x (sigmaIncl B S hS U i)).symm.trans
          (h.trans ((toScheme B S hS).map_comp y (sigmaIncl B S hS U j)))
      exact ⟨Over.isInitialOfIsInitialLeft (Y := Y)
        (isInitial_schemeBelow B
          (isInitial_iff_isEmpty.mpr (isEmpty_of_commSq_sigmaι_of_ne ⟨hxy'⟩ hij)).some)⟩)

/-- **The atlas mechanism of Stacks 02WQ.** If `V` is a coproduct in the big fppf site of `S`
of a family `U`, then the representable sheaf of `V` is the coproduct, in sheaves, of
the representable sheaves of the `U i`.

Consequently a family of morphisms `h_{U i} ⟶ F` into a sheaf `F` assembles into a single
morphism `h_V ⟶ F`, which is what produces the atlas of a coproduct of algebraic spaces. -/
noncomputable def isColimit_yoneda_cofan
    [(BigFppfOver.topology B S hS).Subcanonical] {V : BigFppfOver B S hS}
    (j : ∀ i, U i ⟶ V) (hV : IsColimit (Cofan.mk V j)) :
    IsColimit (Cofan.mk ((BigFppfOver.topology B S hS).yoneda.obj V)
      fun i => (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS).yoneda.map (j i)) := by
  let J := BigFppfOver.topology B S hS
  let e : sigmaObj B S hS U ≅ V :=
    (isColimit_sigmaCofan B S hS U).coconePointUniqueUpToIso hV
  refine Cofan.isColimitOfIso (isColimit_yoneda_sigmaCofan B S hS U) (J.yoneda.mapIso e) ?_
  intro i
  have hfac : sigmaIncl B S hS U i ≫ e.hom = j i :=
    IsColimit.comp_coconePointUniqueUpToIso_hom
      (isColimit_sigmaCofan B S hS U) hV (Discrete.mk i)
  rw [← hfac]
  exact (J.yoneda.map_comp _ _).symm

end BigFppfOver

